    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d161">

                <pb facs="0209" n="193" sameAs="frus:frus1948v09/pg193"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.00B/6–2148</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                            Diplomatic Representatives in the American
                            Republics
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-06-21">June 21, 1948</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Secretary of State transmits herewith for the information and guidance of the
                    Officers in Charge a copy of Policy Planning Staff paper no. 26, dated March 22,
                    1948 entitled: “To establish U.S. policy regarding anti-Communist measures which
                    could be planned and carried out within the Inter-American System.” The
                    Secretary of State approves the conclusions and recommendations in this
                    paper.</p>
                <p>There is likewise enclosed for convenient reference a copy of the resolution
                    approved at the Ninth International Conference of American States at
                        Bogotá<anchor n="1" xml:id="d161-f1"/> on the same subject.</p>



                <xi:include href="d161-a1.xml" xpointer="d161-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d161-a2.xml" xpointer="d161-a2"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d161-f1" n="1" xml:id="d161-f1-content">
                <p>For documentation on this Conference, see <ref target="#pg1">pp. 1</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
